00:00:06,764 --> 00:00:11,657
It replaces that course's older statements
that privileged approval, patient field

4
00:00:11,657 --> 00:00:15,966
protection and managed offline operations
are unfinished.

5
00:00:15,966 --> 00:00:19,478
The original course remains a dated
recording.

6
00:00:19,478 --> 00:00:24,800
These cards explain the current workflow;
they are not recordings of clicks.

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,478
Practise with invented records.

8
00:00:27,478 --> 00:00:32,089
Hospital deployment and live messaging
still require commissioning.

9
00:00:32,808 --> 00:00:37,438
On your first visit, use the guided help
invitation to explore the available

10
00:00:37,438 --> 00:00:38,948
workspace.

11
00:00:38,948 --> 00:00:43,698
Next advances the pointer; close or skip
returns you to work.

12
00:00:43,698 --> 00:00:46,853
You can reopen help when you feel lost.

13
00:00:46,853 --> 00:00:49,698
Available steps follow your role.

14
00:00:49,698 --> 00:00:54,258
The browser remembers the tour preference,
so shared computers may already have

15
00:00:54,258 --> 00:00:55,912
dismissed it.

16
00:00:55,912 --> 00:01:01,496
This is navigation help, not proof that an
employee completed mandatory training.

17
00:01:01,496 --> 00:01:04,965
Check your hospital and branch before
working.

18
00:01:05,683 --> 00:01:10,099
Privileged appointment and recovery now
require independent approval and

19
00:01:10,099 --> 00:01:14,121
target-controlled activation in the
production workflow.

20
00:01:14,121 --> 00:01:18,680
Submit the intended change, have a
different authorised approver review it,

21
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:22,894
and let the intended account holder
complete activation.

22
00:01:22,894 --> 00:01:26,502
Never share activation or recovery
material.

23
00:01:26,502 --> 00:01:29,978
A pending request is not active access.

24
00:01:29,978 --> 00:01:34,525
The public synthetic demo has
demonstration-specific behaviour; do not

25
00:01:34,525 --> 00:01:39,180
copy its credentials or shortcuts into a
hospital deployment.

26
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:43,912
Suspected account changes belong with your
security responder.

27
00:01:44,642 --> 00:01:50,544
In My account security notices, choose a
private email address only you can read.

28
00:01:50,544 --> 00:01:55,056
Send the verification code, then verify
that address.

29
00:01:55,056 --> 00:02:00,282
Account changes use the previously
verified private channel for warnings.

30
00:02:00,282 --> 00:02:05,294
Operators review security events,
investigate scope, take ownership, and

31
00:02:05,294 --> 00:02:08,842
follow escalation and acknowledgement
status.

32
00:02:08,842 --> 00:02:11,687
Sent is different from acknowledged.

33
00:02:11,687 --> 00:02:15,103
An unexpected change needs investigation.

34
00:02:15,103 --> 00:02:20,199
Alerts help detect suspicious activity;
they cannot promise that every data leak

35
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:22,007
will be detected.

36
00:02:22,725 --> 00:02:27,486
Patient field protection now includes
encrypted stored fields, protected lookup

37
00:02:27,486 --> 00:02:30,996
indexes, migration and key rotation.

38
00:02:30,996 --> 00:02:35,555
Ordinary staff continue using their
authorised patient screens.

39
00:02:35,555 --> 00:02:39,377
Only designated operators should run
maintenance.

40
00:02:39,377 --> 00:02:44,317
Verify the selected hospital, protected
backups and paired key versions before

41
00:02:44,317 --> 00:02:46,508
rotation or restore.

42
00:02:46,508 --> 00:02:51,686
Check completed migration and rotation
evidence; do not delete old key versions

43
00:02:51,686 --> 00:02:55,103
while retained records or backups need
them.

44
00:02:55,103 --> 00:03:00,785
Never copy key material into a support
ticket, screenshot or training recording.

45
00:03:01,517 --> 00:03:06,088
A provisioned managed branch node can
retain encrypted local records and buffer

46
00:03:06,088 --> 00:03:10,290
supported intake, corrections, consent
captures and withdrawals during

47
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:11,943
disconnection.

48
00:03:11,943 --> 00:03:16,050
Pending local work is not a globally
enforced decision.

49
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:20,562
Reconnect the managed node, inspect
synchronisation results, and send

50
00:03:20,562 --> 00:03:23,407
conflicts to an authorised reviewer.

51
00:03:23,407 --> 00:03:27,300
A delayed grant must not override a
withdrawal.

52
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:32,371
Do not create an independent database
writer or manually copy database files

53
00:03:32,371 --> 00:03:34,288
between branches.

54
00:03:34,288 --> 00:03:39,097
Your ordinary browser tab alone is not a
managed branch node.

55
00:03:39,808 --> 00:03:44,677
Patients with verified access can withdraw
from home using their patient account;

56
00:03:44,677 --> 00:03:48,174
returning to reception is not the only
route.

57
00:03:48,174 --> 00:03:53,162
Help people without a private phone
through the approved assisted process.

58
00:03:53,162 --> 00:03:58,210
Keep each purpose separate, and never
treat an OTP alone as consent to every

59
00:03:58,210 --> 00:03:59,460
use.

60
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:04,841
After withdrawal, review downstream
acknowledgement and retention decisions.

61
00:04:04,841 --> 00:04:09,579
For existing workflows, continue with the
dated course chapters.

62
00:04:09,579 --> 00:04:14,662
Before real use, your team must commission
providers, hosting, responders and

63
00:04:14,662 --> 00:04:17,148
approved hospital notices.
